# The dock's USB 2.0 half (VIA 2109:2813) enumerates on the PCH controller even
# when its SuperSpeed half fails on the Thunderbolt controller, because Apple
# routes the Type-C port's USB 2.0 pair to the PCH and its SuperSpeed lanes
# through Thunderbolt. That makes the USB 2.0 hub's arrival a reliable "the dock
# was just plugged in" signal, available in exactly the case where nothing on
# the Thunderbolt side fires at all.
#
# dock-superspeed-check.service waits, then checks whether 17e9:6000 turned up,
# and only resets the controller if it did not. A clean plug is a no-op.
#
# The dock contains two of these hubs, so this fires twice; the recovery script
# takes a lock and exits early on the second run.

ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTR{idVendor}=="2109", ATTR{idProduct}=="2813", TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="dock-superspeed-check.service"
